  "notes": "Beijing’s cultural heritage office records a small preserved courtyard house with three bays to north and south and two per side. The museum’s own research office gives the layout and area of the rear writing room. Shizhao’s Qualla original shows the historic threshold and No. 21 plaque. EditQ’s two exact public-domain dedications show the exterior court of the permanent exhibition and its three-bay glazed pavilion."
